extends RefCounted
## The birds of Flathead Lake: what the game does with each, and the real
## facts the bird guide shows beside it, kept apart.
##
## Status, and so how often each turns up in the game, follows Daniel's
## list of the Flathead Valley's birds (from Flathead Audubon, eBird and the
## Flathead River to Lake birding guide). Real sizes, food, nests and seasons
## are general facts of each species, as given by the Cornell Lab's All
## About Birds; local notes are from Montana sources named on each page.
##
## Each species:
##   name, latin, status (Abundant, Common, Uncommon, Rare, Accidental)
##   seasons: when it is here in the game; habitats: where it spawns
##   flock: [fewest, most] in a group; motion: how it moves (birds.gd)
##   length: m, beak to tail, for its model; wings: wingspan m
##   look: [body, wings, head, belly, beak] colours; shape: "song", "duck",
##         "goose", "raptor", "wader", "crow", "grebe", "swan", "hummer", "woodpecker"
##   nest: kind of nest in the game (birds.gd builds them), "" for none
##   game: where to look and what its nest is like, in the game
##   real: {"size", "food", "nest", "breeding", "migration", "local", "fact", "sources"}

